def caesar_cipher(text: str, shift: int) -> str:
    result = []
    for char in text:
        if char.isalpha():
            ascii_offset = 65 if char.isupper() else 97
            shifted_char = chr((ord(char) - ascii_offset + shift) % 26 + ascii_offset)
            result.append(shifted_char)
        else:
            result.append(char)
    return ''.join(result)
```

This function can be used to encrypt messages by shifting the letters in the text by a specified number of positions in the alphabet.

